 "notes": "Headline observed bound: HST 606 nm cosmic optical background anisotropy constraint on decaying blue-axion cold dark matter (axion = 100% of CDM, Omega_CDM h^2 = 0.12, cosmological abundance; no local-halo density involved, so no rho_DM rescaling). Curve extracted from the vector paths of Fig. 9 upper-left panel (e-print Fig9a.pdf), the solid blue 'HST 606 nm' line giving the bound directly on the coupling g (= g_agamma for a->gamma gamma, Eq. 1). Axis calibration verified against the HB-star line at g=0.65e-10 GeV^-1; cross-checked against Fig. 1 (decay-rate plane) via Gamma = g^2 m^3/(64 pi), agreement <1%. This is the paper's conservative bound (Cl not exceeding the upper error bar of any HST data point); the 95% CL likelihood analysis (Fig. 8) strengthens the rate by only ~15-25% (<12% in g). The 438 nm and 336 nm curves are projections and were not used. Scenario chosen: CDM (misalignment); freeze-out/hot-relic/domain-wall variants give weaker bounds and are not reported.",
